        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otranto%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was known as Bartlett's Grove during the 1870s after Mary Bartlett platted the area in 1877.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otranto%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Otranto once called itself Otranto Station due to the proximity of a local railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otranto%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The old Otranto general store featured a dance hall on the second floor and living quarters.",
